        "y" : 0.10199999999999999
      },
      "id" : "p0.l2",
      "text" : "Mitosis: How Cells Divide"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.025000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.71199999999999997,
        "x" : 0.083000000000000004,
        "y" : 0.14799999999999999
      },
      "id" : "p0.l3",
      "text" : "Mitosis is the process by which a single eukaryotic cell divides to produce two"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.028000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.73699999999999999,
        "x" : 0.080000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.16600000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l4",
      "text" : "identical daughter cells. It allows organisms to grow, replace damaged cells and"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.029000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.754,
        "x" : 0.080000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.184
      },
      "id" : "p0.l5",
      "text" : "maintain healthy tissues. During mitosis, the genetic material (DNA) is copied and"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.021999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.36199999999999999,
        "x" : 0.081000000000000003,
        "y" : 0.20300000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l6",
      "text" : "equally separated into two new nuclei."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.021000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.32200000000000001,
        "x" : 0.081000000000000003,
        "y" : 0.22900000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l7",
      "text" : "Mitosis occurs in four main phases:"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.017000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.086999999999999994,
        "x" : 0.13300000000000001,
        "y" : 0.26700000000000002
      },
      "id" : "p0.l8",
      "text" : "Prophase"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.017000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.096000000000000002,
        "x" : 0.33800000000000002,
        "y" : 0.26900000000000002
      },
      "id" : "p0.l9",
      "text" : "Metaphase"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.017000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.085000000000000006,
        "x" : 0.54200000000000004,
        "y" : 0.27300000000000002
      },
      "id" : "p0.l10",
      "text" : "Anaphase"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.014999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.088999999999999996,
        "x" : 0.73599999999999999,
        "y" : 0.27500000000000002
      },
      "id" : "p0.l11",
      "text" : "Telophase"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.014,
        "w" : 0.19,
        "x" : 0.080000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.41499999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l12",
      "text" : "• Chromosomes condense"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.183,
        "x" : 0.29399999999999998,
        "y" : 0.41699999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l13",
      "text" : "• Chromosomes line up at"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.010999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.159,
        "x" : 0.499,
        "y" : 0.41799999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l14",
      "text" : "• Sister chromatids are"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.17399999999999999,
        "x" : 0.69699999999999995,
        "y" : 0.41799999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l15",
      "text" : "• New nuclear envelopes"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.13900000000000001,
        "x" : 0.096000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.432
      },
      "id" : "p0.l16",
      "text" : "and become visible."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.14999999999999999,
        "x" : 0.312,
        "y" : 0.432
      },
      "id" : "p0.l17",
      "text" : "the equator of the cell."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.159,
        "x" : 0.51600000000000001,
        "y" : 0.434
      },
      "id" : "p0.l18",
      "text" : "pulled to opposite poles"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.01,
        "w" : 0.16300000000000001,
        "x" : 0.71499999999999997,
        "y" : 0.433
      },
      "id" : "p0.l19",
      "text" : "form around each set of"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.17000000000000001,
        "x" : 0.078,
        "y" : 0.45200000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l20",
      "text" : "• The nuclear envelope"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.01,
        "w" : 0.17599999999999999,
        "x" : 0.29199999999999998,
        "y" : 0.45200000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l21",
      "text" : "• Spindle fibres attach to"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.01,
        "w" : 0.070000000000000007,
        "x" : 0.51600000000000001,
        "y" : 0.44900000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l22",
      "text" : "of the cell."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.01,
        "w" : 0.10000000000000001,
        "x" : 0.71699999999999997,
        "y" : 0.44900000000000001
      },
      "id" : "p0.l23",
      "text" : "chromosomes."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.096000000000000002,
        "x" : 0.096000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.46600000000000003
      },
      "id" : "p0.l24",
      "text" : "breaks down."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.010999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.11600000000000001,
        "x" : 0.311,
        "y" : 0.46800000000000003
      },
      "id" : "p0.l25",
      "text" : "the centromeres."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.0089999999999999993,
        "w" : 0.18099999999999999,
        "x" : 0.499,
        "y" : 0.46899999999999997
      },
      "id" : "p0.l26",
      "text" : "• Each chromatid becomes"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.010999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.17199999999999999,
        "x" : 0.69899999999999995,
        "y" : 0.46800000000000003
      },
      "id" : "p0.l27",
      "text" : "• Chromosomes unwind"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.012,
        "w" : 0.161,
        "x" : 0.51600000000000001,
        "y" : 0.48399999999999999
      },
      "id" : "p0.l28",
      "text" : "a separate chromosome."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.010999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.14399999999999999,
        "x" : 0.71699999999999997,
        "y" : 0.48399999999999999
      },
      "id" : "p0.l29",
      "text" : "and the cells begin to"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.010999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.063,
        "x" : 0.71899999999999997,
        "y" : 0.5
      },
      "id" : "p0.l30",
      "text" : "separate."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.025000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.41799999999999998,
        "x" : 0.070000000000000007,
        "y" : 0.55100000000000005
      },
      "id" : "p0.l31",
      "text" : "What happens after mitosis?"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.019,
        "w" : 0.76900000000000002,
        "x" : 0.068000000000000005,
        "y" : 0.58299999999999996
      },
      "id" : "p0.l32",
      "text" : "After mitosis, cytokinesis takes place. This is the division of the cytoplasm, producing"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.019,
        "w" : 0.80000000000000004,
        "x" : 0.068000000000000005,
        "y" : 0.60299999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l33",
      "text" : "two separate daughter cells. Each daughter cell is genetically identical to the parent cell,"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.016,
        "w" : 0.377,
        "x" : 0.068000000000000005,
        "y" : 0.625
      },
      "id" : "p0.l34",
      "text" : "with the same number of chromosomes."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.025999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.379,
        "x" : 0.068000000000000005,
        "y" : 0.66000000000000003
      },
      "id" : "p0.l35",
      "text" : "Why is mitosis important?"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.025999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.82599999999999996,
        "x" : 0.067000000000000004,
        "y" : 0.68799999999999994
      },
      "id" : "p0.l36",
      "text" : "Mitosis is essential for growth and development, allowing multicellular organisms to increase"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.021000000000000001,
        "w" : 0.81299999999999994,
        "x" : 0.065000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.71099999999999997
      },
      "id" : "p0.l37",
      "text" : "their number of cells. It also replaces old or damaged cells, such as skin cells, and helps with"
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.021999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.76000000000000001,
        "x" : 0.065000000000000002,
        "y" : 0.72899999999999998
      },
      "id" : "p0.l38",
      "text" : "healing after injury. In unicellular organisms, mitosis is a form of asexual reproduction."
    },
    {
      "box" : {
        "h" : 0.021999999999999999,
        "w" : 0.47299999999999998,
        "x" : 0.081000000000000003,
        "y" : 0.77400000000000002
      },
      "id" : "p0.l39",
      "text" : "Key term: Cytokinesis - the division of the cytoplasm."
    }
  ],
  "width" : 1200
}
